# Trivy accepted-risk register (SEC-CI-001).
#
# Applied to the *gating* steps of .github/workflows/trivy.yml only, never to the
# SARIF steps. A suppression therefore stops a finding blocking a pull request but
# leaves it visible under Security > Code scanning, so nothing disappears quietly.
#
# One CVE per line, and every entry needs a comment saying who accepted it, why,
# and when it should be revisited. An entry with no expiry is a decision nobody
# will ever revisit.
#
# Format:
#   CVE-2024-12345 exp:2026-12-31   # <who> — <why it is not exploitable here>
#
# Note: advisories with no fixed version published are already excluded from the
# gate by `ignore-unfixed: true`. They do not need an entry here.
